<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal firm, oil steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal firm, oil steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were firm in plant delivery condition on limited availability on Thursday, dealers said. Arrivals was limited in central Indian markets.</p>
<p>Some markets were closed for the Diwali holiday and some markets will be closed from tomorrow. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in thin trading but the undertone was dull. Volumes were also limited.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction were firm on better export demand. Soymeal yellow was $267-268 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $128-129 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,300-4,325 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
